% Epoprostenol for Ida's idiopathic pulmonary arterial hypertension: the
% pump K0455 (claim 1), the drug (claim 2) and its cassettes (claim 3) are
% covered; a second K0455 kept as a backup is not (claim 4); treprostinil
% for Jo through an E0781 pump is not (claim 5, and so neither the pump nor
% the drug).
scenario pulmonary_hypertension is:
    claim 1 is for the ambulatory pump.
    the HCPCS code of the ambulatory pump is "K0455".
    the ambulatory pump is furnished to Ida.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the epoprostenol.
    the HCPCS code of the epoprostenol is "J1325".
    the epoprostenol is administered with the ambulatory pump.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 3 is for the cassettes.
    the HCPCS code of the cassettes is "A4222".
    the cassettes is an accessory of the ambulatory pump.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 4 is for the backup pump.
    the HCPCS code of the backup pump is "K0455".
    the backup pump is furnished to Ida.
    the backup pump is a backup pump.
    the epoprostenol is administered with the backup pump.
    the rental month of claim 4 is 1.
    the finding qualifying pulmonary hypertension etiology about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "idiopathic pulmonary arterial hypertension; echocardiogram and pulmonary function tests exclude left heart and lung disease".
    the finding pulmonary hypertension progressed despite treatment about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "functional class IV despite sildenafil and ambrisentan".
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of Ida at rest is 52 mm Hg.
    the finding significant pulmonary hypertension symptoms about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "dyspnea on minimal exertion with syncope".
    the finding calcium channel blockers excluded about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "negative vasoreactivity test".
    claim 5 is for the electric pump.
    the HCPCS code of the electric pump is "E0781".
    the electric pump is furnished to Jo.
    the rental month of claim 5 is 1.
    the treprostinil is administered with the electric pump.
    the HCPCS code of the treprostinil is "J3285".
    the finding qualifying pulmonary hypertension etiology about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "pulmonary arterial hypertension of scleroderma".
    the finding pulmonary hypertension progressed despite treatment about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "worse on two oral agents".
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of Jo at rest is 40 mm Hg.
    the finding significant pulmonary hypertension symptoms about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "dyspnea and fatigability".
    the finding calcium channel blockers excluded about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "not vasoreactive".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Subcutaneous immune globulin: Hizentra (J1559) with an E0779 pump for
% Kim's chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy, which responded
% to intravenous immune globulin — the pump (claim 1) and the drug (claim
% 2) are covered; HyQvia (J1575) given with an E0779 pump for Lee, a
% combination the Article's table does not list (claim 3, not covered);
% Cuvitru (J1555) for Mia's common variable immunodeficiency where the
% reviewer finds home administration unsupported (claim 4, not covered);
% Cuvitru billed for Ned with no pump at all (claim 5, not covered: a drug
% only as a supply to a pump).
scenario immune_globulin is:
    claim 1 is for the mechanical pump.
    the HCPCS code of the mechanical pump is "E0779".
    the mechanical pump is furnished to Kim.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the hizentra.
    the HCPCS code of the hizentra is "J1559".
    the hizentra is administered with the mechanical pump.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Kim is "G61.81".
    the chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy of Kim responded to intravenous immune globulin.
    Kim receives the immune globulin in the home.
    the finding home immune globulin administration appropriate about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "stable on weekly infusions at home; trained caregiver".
    claim 3 is for the second mechanical pump.
    the HCPCS code of the second mechanical pump is "E0779".
    the second mechanical pump is furnished to Lee.
    the rental month of claim 3 is 1.
    the hyqvia is administered with the second mechanical pump.
    the HCPCS code of the hyqvia is "J1575".
    the diagnosis code of Lee is "D83.9".
    Lee receives the immune globulin in the home.
    the finding home immune globulin administration appropriate about Lee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "infusions at home since 2024".
    claim 4 is for the third mechanical pump.
    the HCPCS code of the third mechanical pump is "E0779".
    the third mechanical pump is furnished to Mia.
    the rental month of claim 4 is 1.
    the cuvitru is administered with the third mechanical pump.
    the HCPCS code of the cuvitru is "J1555".
    the diagnosis code of Mia is "D83.9".
    Mia receives the immune globulin in the home.
    the finding home immune globulin administration appropriate about Mia is unsupported, according to the reviewer, because "the record gives no reason for home rather than infusion-center administration and notes repeated infusion reactions".
    claim 5 is for the second cuvitru.
    the HCPCS code of the second cuvitru is "J1555".
    the second cuvitru is furnished to Ned.
    claim 5 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ned is "D83.9".
    Ned receives the immune globulin in the home.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The complete insulin pump claim without proof of delivery: reasonable and
% necessary, not payable; the flip adds the proof.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the insulin pump.
    the HCPCS code of the insulin pump is "E0784".
    the insulin pump is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "E10.9".
    the connecting peptide level of Ann is 80 percent of the lower limit of normal.
    the fasting blood sugar of Ann at the connecting peptide test is 180 mg per dl.
    Ann has completed a comprehensive diabetes education program.
    Ann took 4 insulin injections per day for 12 months before the insulin pump.
    the finding frequent insulin dose self adjustment about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "her log shows correction doses and carbohydrate-ratio adjustments at most meals over the past year".
    Ann self tested glucose an average of 5 times per day during the two months before the insulin pump.
    the glycosylated hemoglobin of Ann on multiple injections is 8.2 percent.
    the insulin pump of Ann is ordered by a practitioner managing multiple beneficiaries on continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion with a knowledgeable team.
    the order for the insulin pump is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the insulin pump is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the insulin pump includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the insulin pump includes order date.
    the order for the insulin pump includes description of the item.
    the order for the insulin pump includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the insulin pump includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the insulin pump was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the insulin pump was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the insulin pump"]].

